# ClassMaterials — what stays out of the class repository.
#
# This file is itself teaching material: the git-collaboration module walks
# through it. Every entry answers "why would committing this hurt a teammate?"

# --- Site and credential detail -------------------------------------------
# zowe.config.json ships with <HOSTNAME>/<TSOID>/<ACCOUNT> placeholders and IS
# tracked, so the repo stays complete. Once you fill it in it carries your
# site's host name and your logon id — details a shared repo should not spread.
# Zowe's answer is a user overlay that git never sees:
zowe.config.user.json
**/zowe.config.user.json
.zowe/

# --- Per-developer editor state -------------------------------------------
# Workspace settings are personal (your DBB HLQ, your USS sandbox path).
.vscode/

# --- Build, debug and scan output -----------------------------------------
# Regenerated on every build; committing it creates conflicts for no benefit.
*.log
logs/
BuildReport.html
BuildReport.json
buildList.txt
.dbb/
dbb-build/
zcodescan-report.*

# --- Local scratch --------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# --- OS clutter -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Eclipse (IDz) project state -------------------------------------------
# The same folder is an IDz Eclipse project. Its compiled output and local
# workspace metadata are per-machine, like .vscode/ above.
bin/
.metadata/
